# Corporate pack — domain registry. This file is the matrix truth.
# Pack: 2026-11-27.1 — illustrative, dated 2026-11-26; not runnable from fabric-ops (ADR 0001).
#
# Copy to <work repo>/config/domains.yaml and edit there. Every value below is a placeholder:
# the all-zero GUID stands for an Entra object ID, and it must be replaced before the first run
# (preflight.py rejects it). Never commit a real tenant, subscription or principal identifier to
# a shared reference; the work repo's own config is the only place a real value belongs.
#
# ONE ROW PER DOMAIN. `name` and `project` are lowercase hyphenated words (contract §2, §3);
# one project per domain. `repo` must be fabric-<name>-nonprod: the nonprod workspace binds to it,
# and prod is never bound (forbid.md rule 8). `owners` are Entra object IDs (users or groups),
# not UPNs and not e-mail addresses; one owner per role is enough to start.
#
# THIS FILE AND THE PIPELINE MUST AGREE. The Build stage asserts that
# `parameters.domains` (the ordered list) and the `parameters.matrix` keys in
# pipelines/cicd.yml match these names exactly — same names, same count, no duplicates —
# and that display_name, project and repo agree (readiness row R2). Add a domain in all
# three places in one change; a name in one place only is the failure R2 exists to catch.
# Owners deliberately do not appear in the pipeline: they are principal identifiers, and
# config/domains.yaml is their only home.
#
# One row produces: one terraform/domains/env/domains.tfvars entry; the
# terraform/workspaces/env/<name>/{nonprod,prod}.tfvars pair; the three group owners; and
# (nonprod only) the Git binding to fabric-<name>-nonprod. Terraform does not read this file
# at plan time — the pipeline materialises the tfvars from it.

domains:
  - name: sales
    display_name: Sales
    project: forecast
    repo: fabric-sales-nonprod
    owners:
      viewers: ["00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]
      contributors: ["00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]
      members: ["00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]

  # A second domain is one more row, plus its rows in the pipeline parameters and the domains
  # root. Copy the shape; do not invent a field the contract does not name.
